This "sum of subarray minimums" code counts, for each element, how many subarrays it is the minimum of. It uses strict `>` when popping on both sides. What does it return for `[1, 1]`, whose correct answer is 3 (subarrays [1], [1], [1, 1])?

```python
def sum_mins(a):
    n = len(a); left = [0]*n; right = [0]*n; st = []
    for i in range(n):
        while st and a[st[-1]] > a[i]: st.pop()
        left[i] = i - st[-1] if st else i + 1
        st.append(i)
    st = []
    for i in range(n - 1, -1, -1):
        while st and a[st[-1]] > a[i]: st.pop()
        right[i] = st[-1] - i if st else n - i
        st.append(i)
    return sum(a[i] * left[i] * right[i] for i in range(n))
```
